🧠 PRD: Conversational Nutrition Companion (v5 – with MVP Scope)

🧩 1. Product Vision

To build an AI-powered nutrition companion that learns your eating patterns, predicts your meals, and helps you stay balanced through an interactive, conversational experience. The app transforms complex nutrition tracking into a natural, intelligent dialogue — one that understands, predicts, and guides you toward your goals for focus, energy, and sustainable weight management.

“It knows what you eat, shows it visually, lets you tweak it, and keeps you on track all day.”

🎯 2. Goals and Success Metrics

CategoryGoalSuccess MetricPrediction AccuracyPredict likely meals accurately≥ 80 % correct ingredient matchEase of TrackingEnable effortless logging via chat or voice90 % successful parsing accuracyPersonalizationAdapt goals based on profile & progress≥ 85 % users complete onboardingSustainabilityReduce fatigue / brain fog70 % report improved focusEngagementMaintain habit consistency≥ 5 active days/week

🧍‍♂️ 3. Target User

Health-focused professionals who want simple yet intelligent nutrition guidance —

Vegetarian + eggs diet preference

Light–moderate activity

1 400–1 700 kcal/day goal

Focused on sustainable weight management, clarity, and efficiency

⚙️ 4. Core Functional Requirements

A. Profile Setup

Conversational onboarding asks:

Height, weight, age, gender

Activity level (definitions included)

Goal (maintain / moderate loss / aggressive loss)

Diet preference (veg / veg + eggs / non-veg)

Meal pattern (3–4/day)

Computes personalized macro goals (e.g., 1 700 kcal → 150P / 120C / 60F / 30 Fiber)

B. Conversational Food Logging

Users enter meals by natural text or voice:

“Lunch: 1 cup Greek yogurt, 1 tsp chia, salad without dressing.”

Recognizes portions, ingredients, brands.

Calculates calories, macros, key micros.

Supports quick edits (“replace oats with quinoa”).

C. Real-Time Nutrient Tracking

Dynamic display:

Calories, Protein, Carbs, Fat, Fiber

Remaining needs (“+22g protein, +30g carbs left”)

Color-coded progress bars (🟢 balanced / 🟠 under / 🔴 over).

Adaptive prompts:

“You’ve hit 85 % fat; keep dinner light on oil.”

“Add leafy greens for iron + magnesium.”

D. End-of-Day Food Fix

At “I’m done for the day,” app analyzes remaining nutrients.

Suggests tailored foods to balance the day (e.g., “½ Barebells bar + Greek yogurt + chia”).

Instant “Add to plan” recalculates totals.

E. Proactive Intelligence

Tracks weekly trends; suggests cheat days and nutrient rotation.

Late-night mode → recommends sleep-safe snacks (<150 kcal).

“Fog alert” when carbs too low or hydration off.

F. Phytonutrient & Micronutrient Diversity

Monitors plant color diversity (greens, oranges, purples, etc.).

Suggests missing color groups for antioxidant balance.

G. Predictive and Visual Enhancements (Phase 2+)

(Future capabilities for roadmap — not MVP)

Predictive meals: suggests likely foods based on history/time.

Visual meal builder: displays editable ingredient tiles.

What-if simulation: shows nutrient changes when swapping foods.

🧮 5. Calculation Logic

Uses verified food databases (USDA + Indian FSSAI + brand APIs).

Dynamic recalculation on add/remove.

Handles household units (cup, tsp, slice).

Adjusts macros automatically for selected goal type.

📊 6. MVP Scope (0–3 Months)

The Minimum Viable Product delivers complete daily tracking, nutrient intelligence, and end-of-day guidance.

CategoryFeatureDescriptionCore InteractionConversational Food LoggingText/voice input, AI parsing of foods, real-time confirmation.PersonalizationProfile SetupActivity level, goal, diet type; auto-calculated macros.AnalyticsNutrient TrackerLive calories and macros summary with remaining balance.GuidanceEnd-of-Day Food FixEnd-of-day gap analysis + closing meal suggestions.EngagementCheat & Snack PromptsLight AI guidance on snacks and weekly cheat frequency.ReportingDaily/Weekly SummaryTrends on calories, macros, fiber, and adherence score.

✅ MVP Deliverables

100 % working conversational loop

Day-level macro tracking + feedback

Onboarding with goal computation

End-of-day nutrient balancing

Simple UI for chat + daily summary view

🚀 MVP Success Criteria

≥ 70 % of users log 5+ meals per week

Average deviation from macro target ≤ 10 %

≥ 80 % satisfaction with daily recommendations

