🧠 8. Example User Experience Flow

Morning:

“Breakfast: 1 egg, 3 whites, 1 chai.” ✅ System logs → 210 kcal, 23 g protein, 17 g carbs.

Afternoon:

“Lunch: 1 cup Greek yogurt, salad, 1 tbsp chia.” App replies: “Lunch logged. You have 950 kcal, 85 g protein left for the day.”

Evening: User says “Done for the day.” App:

“You’re short 14 g protein and 5 g fiber. Add ½ Barebells bar + yogurt for balance.” Click → Totals updated → summary chart shown.

🔔 9. Notifications / Prompts

TimeContextExample8 a.m.Missed breakfast“Add your usual eggs and chai?”3 p.m.Fatigue detected“Try a protein snack for steady focus.”9 p.m.Late hunger“½ cup Greek yogurt + chia = perfect closeout.”SundayWeekly recap“Avg: 1 540 kcal/day, 142 g protein. Excellent consistency.”

📈 10. Future Enhancements

Predictive AI (meal memory + time-based suggestion)

Visual ingredient composer

Pantry-aware end-of-day planning

Focus-energy analytics dashboard

Smart nutrition simulation (“if I eat this…”)

✅ 11. Summary

This version of the PRD establishes a clear MVP foundation:

Conversational logging

Personalized daily macro tracking

Real-time nutrient guidance

End-of-day balancing suggestions

and evolves toward a predictive, visual, and context-aware nutrition coach in later phases.

The MVP focuses on core daily value — “Log easily, know what’s missing, fix it fast” — while later phases build intelligence, automation, and personalization for sustainable health and focus.

